Message-ID: <156524537457.3391.10849701988135714001.reportbug@sputnik.fam-tille.de>

Package: release.debian.org
Severity: normal
User: release.debian.org at packages.debian.org
Usertags: rm

(explain the reason for the removal here)

Please remove r-bioc-metagenomeseq from testing.  It would block the
migration of R packages otherwise.  The reason is that we can not
upgrade r-bioc-metagenomeseq to the new upstream version since it got a
new dependency from a non-free package.  We are sorting this out with
upstream but this might take time.  All other r-bioc packages are
depending from the virtual package r-api-bioc-3.9 while
r-bioc-metagenomeseq 1.24.1-1 depends r-api-bioc-3.8.  So there is a
conflicting dependency which can only be resolved by a temporary removal
of r-bioc-metagenomeseq 1.24.1-1 from testing.

Kind regards

      Andreas.

